NAME
       close - close a file descriptor

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int close(int fd);

DESCRIPTION
       Releases FD. The underlying file is only let go once the last
       descriptor referring to it is closed, which is what makes dup
       and fork safe.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set on failure.

ERRORS
       EBADF   fd is not an open descriptor

SEE ALSO
       open(2), dup(2), read(2), write(2)
